  "task": "Set up a weekly flash report template that automatically calculates week-to-date and month-to-date figures. Pull data from the daily transaction log sheet, show the key metrics, and protect the template structure so only the input cells can be edited. The report should look polished — proper fonts, colors, and layout. The file to work on is /home/user/calc_fin_weekly_flash_report_080_initial.xlsx.\n\nRequirements (every item is checked; keep the existing sheet names DailyLog and FlashReport):\n1. DailyLog: fill Gross Profit for every data row with a formula Revenue minus COGS, i.e. E2:E31 = B-D on the same row (e.g. =B2-D2).\n2. FlashReport A1: the text \"Weekly Flash Report\", merged across A1:H1, bold, font size at least 14 pt (16 pt suggested), white text (#FFFFFF) on a solid dark blue fill (red < 60, green < 80, blue > 60, e.g. #1F3864).\n3. FlashReport A2 = \"Week of:\"; B2 = a formula using TODAY() and WEEKDAY that returns the Monday of the current week, e.g. =TODAY()-WEEKDAY(TODAY(),2)+1.\n4. Row 4 headers in A4:H4, exactly: Metric | Mon | Tue | Wed | Thu | Fri | WTD Total | MTD Total.\n5. Metric labels in A5:A8, exactly: Revenue, Orders, COGS, Gross Profit.\n6. Each of the 20 cells B5:F8 is an IFERROR(VLOOKUP(...)) formula that looks up that day (B2 + 0..4) in the DailyLog sheet and returns the matching metric column (the formula must contain IFERROR, VLOOKUP and DailyLog).\n7. G5:G8 = SUM of the row's Mon-Fri cells (e.g. =SUM(B5:F5)); H5:H8 = month-to-date totals computed with SUMPRODUCT or SUMIF(S) over the DailyLog sheet.\n8. Alternating row shading on rows 5-8: rows 5 and 7 share one fill color, rows 6 and 8 share a different one (checked in column A). The WTD Total cell for Revenue (G5) uses a dollar currency format (contains \"$\"); the Orders WTD cell (G6) must not use a currency format.\n9. Enable sheet protection on FlashReport, with B2 left unlocked so the week selector stays editable.\n10. Save the workbook in place at the same path, keeping the .xlsx format.",
